    "durationMs": 126707,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. \n\n**What I built:**\n- `app/main.py` — FastAPI routes: `POST /links` (201 with generated or custom code, 409 on duplicates), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (302 with a single `UPDATE clicks = clicks + 1` before responding), and `GET /links` (ascending by id with `total`). Custom exception handlers ensure every error response (422/404/409/500) has an `error` field.\n- `app/schemas.py` — manual URL validation (absolute http/https with host, returned unchanged — no pydantic URL normalization) and the `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$` code rule enforced on both the POST body and path params.\n- `app/db.py` + `app/config.py` — SQLAlchemy 2.1 with the psycopg 3 driver; connection string read from `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials).\n- `migrations/` — Alembic migration creating the `links` table; `start.sh` runs `python -m alembic upgrade head` then `exec`s uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground.\n- `requirements.txt` with the exact stack pins and a README \"Running the server\" section.\n\n**Verification:** a 28-check httpx suite passed covering every requirement (including URL-unchanged, click incrementing exactly once, malformed JSON, and list ordering). I restarted the server twice — links and click counts survived, and re-running migrations was a no-op. The database is left clean and no background processes remain."
